      "message": "Group badge-definition queries by author to fix large NIP-51 badge sets\n\nThe badge grid in feed cards rendered as anonymous placeholders for any\nset with more than a handful of entries — e.g. RetroAchievements game\nsets with 100+ badges. BadgeSetContent (and the shared\nuseBadgeDefinitions hook) built one filter per badge reference, so a\n122-badge set issued one REQ with 122 filters. Many relays cap filters\nper subscription well below that, so the query returned empty or was\ndropped, badgeMap stayed empty, and every tile fell through to the\ngeneric Award icon with the slugified d-tag as its label.\n\nGroup refs by author and emit one filter per author with the full list\nof identifiers in `#d`. For a single-issuer set that collapses 122\nfilters into one round-trip; multi-issuer sets still get one filter per\ndistinct author. Also drop BadgeSetContent's duplicate query in favor of\nthe shared hook so future improvements land in both places.\n\nRegression-of: f3edd02c",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "6dcb5ab1555964df8b5e05bb184050c8e5241645",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/soapbox-pub/ditto/git/trees/6dcb5ab1555964df8b5e05bb184050c8e5241645"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/soapbox-pub/ditto/git/commits/36cd9142863d5c21c23b61e8f0e7556d870d5e11",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEESof9JJzQIzN3kpf4chHR+ZdE+7cFAmoGeaMACgkQchHR+ZdE\n+7elURAAoR2mMNbp7zT0gIwZhOgOG1KBJlmmQqGswnEwrHngmS7njL7U70XjlLfd\nDuPCpnJltTXQNWiW8JPpRoZ9phshPirWZHJz+vPicv7LInhJCBbm5NXGbZuaNXLv\nEc6rK7YHXhUuzeCMxEKiVuH48StSnshZ7axdjyb07wWArv/nXU9PLmXeg7wufT86\njRzgooYk+V2iXkZgx3IhIEg8YvwhFZKf3/UaQU58JQKgpAzl2V+BqRMt3Fhm3iNq\nugTFlgCmAnfBXE+1SDE1isAGxusU0+jbjv4BwH+uyEkzYsPi5WyIVvjk+l4k67UN\nnQL9yENGrQJeBTxDcWvEmbcgnUVJFmMeIebJ0kYK9cJ3Cvjim1zk1mLewdF4m3/X\nrkFluQzp60RooUJ5xLE4wy7b7Wv2niW/X474X3/GxwWQTuk6RI8yziCBkVZXRX9s\nul32QyEOzFWNehPCQDx2ZCsIt1A9EOSuSsMzstJDnnLRmi4QdN+x/As0Q1hIpybq\nShShNuxJeI6MN8fDE8AsZoh/XciWkvS/k1fEjIcThEsmkOPL97ZZv65jdyk6oHo6\nYMgqPjbxleEMtPt00GELVucKScKbvOQl9osXCfi8+tuXSs0zYqStg7EDAzVJsLOY\nFMzkKefXWM0SkWRKAKzViTlYGR6mUPSGi1gz+rR2WBP/fYwW6xc=\n=nj0r\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----",
        "payload": "tree 6dcb5ab1555964df8b5e05bb184050c8e5241645\nparent 9159a015692f68b73d19f474c3c20da92fbf8c67\nauthor Alex Gleason <alex@alexgleason.me> 1778809251 -0500\ncommitter Alex Gleason <alex@alexgleason.me> 1778809251 -0500\n\nGroup badge-definition queries by author to fix large NIP-51 badge sets\n\nThe badge grid in feed cards rendered as anonymous placeholders for any\nset with more than a handful of entries — e.g. RetroAchievements game\nsets with 100+ badges. BadgeSetContent (and the shared\nuseBadgeDefinitions hook) built one filter per badge reference, so a\n122-badge set issued one REQ with 122 filters. Many relays cap filters\nper subscription well below that, so the query returned empty or was\ndropped, badgeMap stayed empty, and every tile fell through to the\ngeneric Award icon with the slugified d-tag as its label.\n\nGroup refs by author and emit one filter per author with the full list\nof identifiers in `#d`. For a single-issuer set that collapses 122\nfilters into one round-trip; multi-issuer sets still get one filter per\ndistinct author. Also drop BadgeSetContent's duplicate query in favor of\nthe shared hook so future improvements land in both places.\n\nRegression-of: f3edd02c\n",
