  {
    "sha": "f3edd02c94da3e7174dc861004e24ece4930f613",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOL5Eek9oAKGYzZWRkMDJjOTRkYTNlNzE3NGRjODYxMDA0ZTI0ZWNlNDkzMGY2MTM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Alex Gleason",
        "email": "alex@alexgleason.me",
        "date": "2026-05-14T23:32:53Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Alex Gleason",
        "email": "alex@alexgleason.me",
        "date": "2026-05-14T23:32:53Z"
      },
      "message": "Render NIP-51 badge sets (kind 30008 with arbitrary d) distinctly from legacy NIP-58 profile badges\n\nKind 30008 is overloaded: NIP-58 originally defined it as profile badges\n(d=profile_badges), and NIP-51 now defines it as 'badge set' — a\ncategorized group of NIP-58 badges with optional title/description/image.\nDitto was treating every 30008 as legacy profile badges, so badge sets\nrendered blank (parseProfileBadges rejects non-profile_badges d-tags)\nand their action header read 'updated their badges' instead of using\nthe set's title.\n\nDiscriminate at the event level via isProfileBadgesEvent / isBadgeSetEvent\nin badgeUtils, add a dedicated BadgeSetContent renderer with the set's\nhero (image + title + description) plus the badge grid, and have the\nfeed action header interpolate the title — so e.g. a Super Mario Bros.\nbadge set reads 'Alice updated Super Mario Bros. badges' with 'badges'\nlinking to /badges. Updates the dispatch in NoteCard, PostDetailPage,\nEmbeddedNote, EmbeddedNaddr, and the label / icon / suffix maps in\nCommentContext, NotificationsPage, and extraKinds so the two variants\nstay separate everywhere a kind label is rendered.",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "5d7583349f78704dce33e64168b24ceafc41c4fd",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/soapbox-pub/ditto/git/trees/5d7583349f78704dce33e64168b24ceafc41c4fd"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/soapbox-pub/ditto/git/commits/f3edd02c94da3e7174dc861004e24ece4930f613",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEESof9JJzQIzN3kpf4chHR+ZdE+7cFAmoGW6UACgkQchHR+ZdE\n+7ddLA/+JpYk9fpG2oIojE3cMY7ETflvULTzJ06SkWsRlFN1tAk+nYdzzHCTf4+P\ncVyglYGcGSSnUotJg+acVFW8eq3ht+hC+5ze9KL8WuyFpVTy1NFdSjXtnh7lsgDw\nE/RLbJOJL5GvXoMLYTGoKcewF0zw3hW4VOmKRAZQe2nB+AJlSY1XQlTcSPiS06n6\n6RuxpO7e7vLL5OPu1+eEiPRGZiB9/o7R47aq2oRxIC3+EwcjLQxWwqhCI+KCd1pg\nws4Q3MugwM/mEaE5KVsdISt8deFJippSq5f4zkl8RkEivQ4ZNoUrpNrmcNL1fm+O\nCpDav+UU0W3IFA5kc+xfNdqH5Y6XiaTP7XHn23O8ixgzY1EB3rYiXCsipogt6EhF\nLJBiWdjgYyOPPJ6WTa87nitwJlDLKt8oi+DB6lyqgmhVT/inRHXfnV0c+59HBf0Z\ni3XzWkfRXRcy5t6vCQnDlrjoalP3f7428G14jgI6wTk6bIUCsiIq9HR47O50M2oc\nf7TNObCbX9q1IyHZ/US+sLX+F0hrchHQBXSry3Q4UyFkMAzqHk7ulRpKjvq9vNsx\neqjs4c4A9+nMOEsbXh2t7enHxKQzsub4qnPJN1lnJ+cnZr/vZAKJxTs7iJVBfC9Q\njWQFejsoDPe5jVvfI3PCM/7Ffkl+vvZHNqw8+au+GVOGCGRDBEE=\n=6YmB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----",
        "payload": "tree 5d7583349f78704dce33e64168b24ceafc41c4fd\nparent 054f1a50ed2b4f2b1bc6925dbb4f8f40b8ec7712\nauthor Alex Gleason <alex@alexgleason.me> 1778801573 -0500\ncommitter Alex Gleason <alex@alexgleason.me> 1778801573 -0500\n\nRender NIP-51 badge sets (kind 30008 with arbitrary d) distinctly from legacy NIP-58 profile badges\n\nKind 30008 is overloaded: NIP-58 originally defined it as profile badges\n(d=profile_badges), and NIP-51 now defines it as 'badge set' — a\ncategorized group of NIP-58 badges with optional title/description/image.\nDitto was treating every 30008 as legacy profile badges, so badge sets\nrendered blank (parseProfileBadges rejects non-profile_badges d-tags)\nand their action header read 'updated their badges' instead of using\nthe set's title.\n\nDiscriminate at the event level via isProfileBadgesEvent / isBadgeSetEvent\nin badgeUtils, add a dedicated BadgeSetContent renderer with the set's\nhero (image + title + description) plus the badge grid, and have the\nfeed action header interpolate the title — so e.g. a Super Mario Bros.\nbadge set reads 'Alice updated Super Mario Bros. badges' with 'badges'\nlinking to /badges. Updates the dispatch in NoteCard, PostDetailPage,\nEmbeddedNote, EmbeddedNaddr, and the label / icon / suffix maps in\nCommentContext, NotificationsPage, and extraKinds so the two variants\nstay separate everywhere a kind label is rendered.\n",
        "verified_at": "2026-05-14T23:36:35Z"
      }
